  "resourceBoundary": {
    "maxRequestBytes": 5246976,
    "maxReadResponseBytes": 5246976,
    "policy": "Complete original encoded UTF8 native request: Copy/Cut/Paste alone allow5246976 bytes (4MiB records+complete order arrays, 4096*256 bounded cell/container reserve,4096 full header reserve); Copy/Cut complete correlated replies use the same limit; Paste compact replies and every other frame operation remain4096. Authenticated TCP and actual MCP nemo_command frames above the unchanged1048574-byte legacy outer limit add at most4096 wrapper bytes; ordinary legacy frames keep their original bound. Native data accounting remains4194304 bytes; no truncation, chunking, fallback or new clipboard owner. Full reply preflight precedes Cut commit. Per-message bounds do not solve pre-existing unbounded lifetime receipt retention. MCP ingress/TCP frame limit is not a stdout limit. Actual SDK structured stdout duplicates native JSON as text plus structuredContent; separately derived conservative resource ceiling16789636 bytes includes escaping, existing admitted outer ID and finalLF, without a new postcommit output gate.",
    "nativeClipboardDataBytes": 4194304,
    "cellAndContainerReserveBytes": 1048576,
    "correlationHeaderReserveBytes": 4096,
    "authenticatedWrapperReserveBytes": 4096,
    "requestBytesByOperation": {
